{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically queried the EHR, elicited current symptoms, verified medication execution, and built an executable plan with follow-up timing, owner, and red-flag contingencies. All six responsibility-chain items are met without error; three of four high-order points (HO1, HO3, HO4) are fully completed with meaningful trajectory impact, while HO2 is only partially completed because one key misunderstanding was not explicitly corrected. This trajectory meets Strong but cannot reach Perfect because only one high-order point is complete beyond the required minimum when HO2 remains partial.",
